cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Representation Overlap Lab: Why Safety Boundaries Are Not Always Cleanly Separable"
message: >-
  If you use this project in research, education, or public communication about AI safety,
  please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ortiz
    given-names: Jacob
    alias: agentjakey
    affiliation: University of California San Diego / American Refrigeration Inc.
    orcid: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/agentjakey/representation-overlap-lab"
url: "https://huggingface.co/spaces/agentjakey/representation-overlap-lab"
abstract: >-
  An interactive AI safety education tool that visualizes how benign, ambiguous, and
  risk-relevant concepts overlap in semantic embedding space. The project is intended to
  help researchers, educators, and policy-curious readers understand why safety boundaries
  are hard to draw cleanly - not because safety systems are broken, but because the
  underlying representational geometry does not respect the categories we want to enforce.
  This is a map for thinking, not a judge.
keywords:
  - AI safety
  - representation learning
  - semantic embeddings
  - interpretability
  - AI alignment education
  - content moderation
